# traces/MANIFEST.sha256 - digests of the generated v2 trace sets (SW §5.6). The data is not in git:
# every set is regenerated byte-identically by its regen.sh from fixed seeds (`traces/<set>/regen.sh
# build/dev`). A set's digest is the sha256 of `sha256sum` over its files (regen.sh excluded) in
# byte-order path order; check one with
#   cd traces && find <set> -type f ! -name regen.sh -print0 | LC_ALL=C sort -z | xargs -0 sha256sum | sha256sum
# The digests are those of the dev host: the generator draws some random inputs through libm
# (normal deviates, the ROPE constants), so another libm may give different bytes.
# A frozen reference set goes into git once the v2 ISA is frozen for the RTL (after the M6 RTL).
# set           files  digest
m2              1258   a89344c8e6c0c7f895623980123f6187f7db3fc5334d2de34b641164c1cc8353
gen             580    751b35079b28824d3d652c696c0ac41a2bdb72ad65c3b226e5305a6a715df50b
vu              1757   854dd8a08ac6db56a846e42560ca7fa13ce18ae57e881ad8afcaa629a7d21f0d
at              4066   30912bc92e84c1a4112862538fe5d4bae025c62ce991eb9057c038cde3f2b84c
ctrl            5811   f044bff08bb8967cbd8e937670c18ec1c9f25eaa357ba64e548d7f867b33c6cb
m3              5189   e1a4937106b4c85f11bbc71e67233b7abe925b7eefb7293bd38d565eab6df16e
model-v1conv    3140   b00e0b4f7007b1ad7ac1ae251b0edd3c83b1d747703946f6da54a10c3fe375c8
